      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/hrhG8x9vN4_JSHRVo-sVG4GBT1gGrMc5BTXExZb3W8Fxdz5v_6mZIVMCIVkEVdcMJ7Kwhdci=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "The Faroe Islands are fascinating because isolation has produced a society that is modern yet still deeply shaped by the North Atlantic. 🌊🇫🇴 Weather can decide travel plans, grass roofs still make practical sense, and tunnels now connect communities that once depended heavily on boats. The tension between preserving island traditions and keeping younger generations from leaving may be one of the most interesting challenges these villages face.",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-08T08:46:40Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Ugx0aP8yr3bshGVczJN4AaABAg",
      "author": "@HomelandJourneys",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/aYTD_LjrCVqE6yKjJDzPjTJQfPw7giBEdmdlIX1TOwbAo0VExPdiguA_3QzCXGqbGWC48k5I=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Those isolated villages make me think about how differently you might measure a good day when the weather shapes all your plans. The cliffs are spectacular, but I’m more interested in the small comforts people come home to when the wind picks up and the sea turns rough.",
      "likeCount": 0,
